{:db/id 17592186184171 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186184070 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/id #uuid "10cc01a6-af19-5340-9743-ade4d5e252dc" :question/math-academy-id "e-5425" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $3\\times 5$ matrix. If $\\mathcal{B}= \\{\\mathbf{b_1}, \\mathbf{b_2}, \\mathbf{b_3}\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Col}(A)$, find $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{rank}(A) + \\textrm{nullity}(A) = n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ and since $\\mathcal{B}$ is formed by $3$ vectors, $\\textrm{rank}(A) = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186048823} {:db/id 17592186049009}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186184759 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c2c253b-eb4a-53cb-b0ca-7c84c3094ed1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186183164} {:answer/id #uuid "a1905378-ce91-51d4-9b0f-bc5b3501e65e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186183165} {:answer/id #uuid "3829fa6b-44cd-591e-a98f-f251876ca514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186183166} {:answer/id #uuid "44fd0839-e352-55e5-a108-928603beaa61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186183167} {:answer/id #uuid "499609e4-1cbc-5b03-a3fc-4d0860e6c9f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186183168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "499609e4-1cbc-5b03-a3fc-4d0860e6c9f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186183168} :answer-field/id #uuid "229b5487-34b1-598b-9b5d-3ffee9c57d59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186183163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "67b28820-a085-5f18-884d-33b6d40e4f35" :question/math-academy-id "q-35306" :question/problem "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+2 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186184760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abafdde9-cae5-582c-8e9f-4abfcfbcb322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :an