 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186272352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2009a374-1d2a-5ba2-ad4a-1a48347f5e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id 17592186269535} {:answer/id #uuid "38917204-aa38-58c1-8e36-7ab9157fb604" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186269781} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf4f2c6-2da0-56d1-945e-c8611cf17b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186269817} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5d7214-9d8d-575e-b4ca-31a2e1ea8f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186271087} {:answer/id #uuid "ff2483b0-86f4-51c4-a8a9-ebc036bb88de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186271500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bf4f2c6-2da0-56d1-945e-c8611cf17b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186269817} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d4dce18-e14e-53dd-b0f4-b089ee7b76ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186271676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7d182fc6-16c7-589f-980f-eb790356faa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-142487" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $6\\times 8$ matrix. If $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},{b}_{4},{b}_{5}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nulli