xt{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$" :question/worked-solution "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=5,$ and since $B$ is formed by $3$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186323675 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d562ea0c-94f3-5fe6-ba82-c651a51d0bbe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b5be7eb-072d-5dbb-85d1-4bb399b16dbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id 17592186321739} {:answer/id #uuid "682f17c8-dc59-5ca2-9a8d-858f8e1d270d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186321960} {:answer/id #uuid "69b23ec7-308e-55f0-87ff-d98810e90a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id 17592186321975} {:answer/id #uuid "d22ac36a-96b4-56fa-bb44-6e52d5841d9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id 17592186322788} {:answer/id #uuid "e52564db-fb76-550d-a946-192a8ea03547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id 17592186322940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "682f17c8-dc59-5ca2-9a8d-858f8e1d270d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id 17592186321960} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9490f7a-31fa-5933-90ba-5b4d669f2d46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186323627}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98e375b6-3e6d-5b62-8ce3-1cf16ed1d92d" :question/math-academy-id "q-35434" :questio